questions.question:
A circus tent is in the shape of a cylinder surmounted by a conical top. If the height and diameter of the cylindrical part are 9 m and 30 m respectively and height of the conical part is 8 m with same diameter as that of the cylindrical part, then find:
(a) the area of the canvas used in making the tent;
(b) the cost of the canvas at the rate ₹200 per sq. m, if 30 sq. m canvas was wasted during stitching.

questions.answer:
E1 = {1,2}, E2 = {4,5,6}
E1 ∪ E2 = {1,2,4,5,6} ≠ S = {1,2,3,4,5,6}
So E1 and E2 are NOT complementary events. Assertion is false.
Reason is true: For complementary events, P(E) + P(F) = 1.
